				"252B1D6D21683A9C"
			]
			description: [
				"Titanium supports spin to 2,048 RPM, four times steel, with no drag, any load and no weathering. Its casing takes a bushing, like aluminium's."
				""
				"The catch: they need twice aluminium's cooling at the same speed, and past 1,000 °C they burn, flaring white and setting fire across the gap, then crumbling to powder. Heat sinks melt long before that, so fast titanium needs water coolers, on cold water or coolant for the top speeds."
				""
				"Heat leaves temper colours, gold, purple and blue, that stay until acid strips them."
			]
			id: "36F8B6611C6A4123"
